prompt:
Explain why the following C++ code compiles but produces unexpected behavior. Identify the bug, fix it, and explain object lifetime and undefined behavior:

#include <iostream>
#include <string>
using namespace std;

const string& getName() {
    string name = "Alex";
    return name;
}

int main() {
    cout << getName() << endl;
}

Review this JavaScript function for race conditions and incorrect state updates. Rewrite it so multiple requests can run concurrently without stale results overwriting newer ones. Explain your approach and include edge-case tests:

let currentResult = null;
async function search(query) {
  const response = await fetch('/api/search?q=' + query);
  const data = await response.json();
  currentResult = data;
  return currentResult;
}
